WEBVTT

0
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.110
As AI clusters scale to thousands of GPUs,

1
00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:09.739
traditional networks are hitting a wall.

2
00:00:10.229 --> 00:00:11.239
Throughout this training,

3
00:00:11.359 --> 00:00:12.819
we will explore exactly

4
00:00:13.109 --> 00:00:15.640
how optical circuit switching breaks through that

5
00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:18.719
wall to fundamentally reshape modern data centers.

6
00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:24.049
What began as a specialized research technology has rapidly

7
00:00:24.049 --> 00:00:27.950
evolved into a cornerstone of hyperscale infrastructure acceleration.

8
00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:32.098
By eliminating electrical bottlenecks,

9
00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:38.340
OCS is providing the massive bandwidth per watt and ultra low latency

10
00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:41.580
required to scale the next generation of AI workloads.

11
00:00:42.889 --> 00:00:45.919
But hardware innovation is only half of the story.

12
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.060
For OCS to truly scale across the industry and

13
00:00:50.419 --> 00:00:52.790
avoid proprietary fragmented solutions,

14
00:00:53.099 --> 00:00:56.419
open standards and interoperability are non-negotiable.

15
00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:00.919
That is why the Open Compute project formed the OCS Working Group.

16
00:01:02.669 --> 00:01:05.750
Our mission is to accelerate OCS adoption

17
00:01:05.989 --> 00:01:08.059
by developing open specifications,

18
00:01:08.169 --> 00:01:09.480
reference architectures,

19
00:01:09.709 --> 00:01:14.739
and interoperability standards for the entire community ranging from AI labs,

20
00:01:14.819 --> 00:01:17.980
hyper-scale data centers to emerging neo clouds.

21
00:01:18.269 --> 00:01:21.455
We are Actively working across multiple fronts.

22
00:01:21.785 --> 00:01:25.894
These work streams include open specifications for OCS hardware,

23
00:01:26.264 --> 00:01:29.425
standardized data models for software control,

24
00:01:29.785 --> 00:01:32.014
software defined networking integration,

25
00:01:32.184 --> 00:01:34.684
and frameworks for data center optimization.

26
00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:39.300
The future of AI networking is being built

27
00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:42.059
right now and it relies on open collaboration.

28
00:01:43.379 --> 00:01:47.680
We invite you to join the OCP OCS subproject and

29
00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:51.239
help us engineer the optical fabric from ground up.

30
00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:56.709
Whether you want to contribute to our technical specs or simply stay informed,

31
00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:00.860
join our project mailing list and attend our regular open working sessions.

32
00:02:01.319 --> 00:02:04.580
Thank you for your partnership on this infrastructure roadmap and

33
00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:06.330
welcome to the OCP community.